  "body": "Since v10.2.0, TypeScript reports an error inside Execa's own declarations when a project enables \`exactOptionalPropertyTypes\` and does not use \`skipLibCheck\`. v10.1.1 type-checks cleanly with the same setup.\\n\\n### Reproduction\\n\\n\`package.json\`:\\n\\n\`\`\`json\\n{\\n  \\"type\\": \\"module\\",\\n  \\"dependencies\\": { \\"execa\\": \\"10.2.0\\" },\\n  \\"devDependencies\\": { \\"@types/node\\": \\"26.6.5\\", \\"typescript\\": \\"7.0.2\\" }\\n}\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n\`tsconfig.json\`:\\n\\n\`\`\`json\\n{\\n  \\"compilerOptions\\": {\\n    \\"strict\\": true,\\n    \\"exactOptionalPropertyTypes\\": true,\\n    \\"module\\": \\"nodenext\\",\\n    \\"target\\": \\"es2022\\",\\n    \\"noEmit\\": true,\\n    \\"skipLibCheck\\": fals… (+1277 chars)",
