  "body": "### Problem\\n\\nWhen a subprocess cannot be spawned, \`execa()\` and \`execaSync()\` disagree about its output:\\n\\n\`\`\`js\\nawait execa('does-not-exist').catch(({stdout, stderr}) => [stdout, stderr]);\\n// ['', '']\\n\\ntry { execaSync('does-not-exist'); } catch ({stdout, stderr}) { /* [undefined, undefined] */ }\\n\`\`\`\\n\\nSame for a \`cwd\` that does not exist, and for every shape of the option:\\n\\n| options | \`execa()\` | \`execaSync()\` |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| *(default)* | \`''\` | \`undefined\` |\\n| \`encoding: 'buffer'\` | \`Uint8Array(0)\` | \`undefined\` |\\n| \`lines: true\` | \`[]\` | \`undefined\` |\\n| \`all: true\` | \`''\` | \`undefin… (+2625 chars)",
